"""matmulfree-tapeout — HGRN-bit (MatMul-free LM) tile controller through
OpenROAD Flow Scripts on the GT2N (2nm GAAFET, Georgia Tech) PDK.

bazel-orfs lives at ./bazel-orfs as a git submodule, pinned to a fork
(github.com/MrPoloGit/bazel-orfs, branch gt2n-support) that adds GT2N
platform support on top of upstream bazel-orfs main.

Override declarations are root-only in bzlmod, so non-dev, non-tag
overrides from bazel-orfs/MODULE.bazel must be re-declared here. Kept
minimal deliberately: start from nothing extra and let Bazel's own
resolution errors say what's actually missing, rather than
hand-transcribing bazel-orfs's full MODULE.bazel (900+ lines, many
dev-only and already dropped for non-root consumers) and risking a
stale copy.
"""

module(
    name = "matmulfree-tapeout",
    version = "0.0.1",
)

bazel_dep(name = "bazel-orfs")
local_path_override(
    module_name = "bazel-orfs",
    path = "bazel-orfs",
)

# Root-only overrides from bazel-orfs/MODULE.bazel that the openroad/yosys
# build chain needs, re-declared verbatim here (comments kept from the
# source of truth) -- the same duplication HighTide/SOFA-orfs's own
# MODULE.bazel does for their (older) bazel-orfs pin; bzlmod honors
# git_override/archive_override/single_version_override only in the root
# module, so every consumer of bazel-orfs must repeat them, regardless of
# which commit it pins. Skipped: the kepler-formal (logic-equivalence,
# dev-only in bazel-orfs/test) override and the llvm/apple_support/flex/
# fmt/rules_cc/rules_cc_autoconf/yaml-cpp/zlib pins that exist only to hold
# versions steady against kepler-formal's own pull -- none of those enter
# this module's graph since we don't depend on it.

